gIq(){return"About this app"},
gIp(){return"A tool for tracking and calculating a match played with real cards \u2014 it doesn't include the cards or rules themselves. In portrait orientation it's meant for two players sharing one device across a table; the top and bottom halves of the screen face each player's own direction. In landscape orientation, it is intended for managing only your side of the field."},
gIs(){return"Card controls"},
gIr(){return"Tap a card to open the damage dialog. Damage changes in 10/50/100 steps, matching the real 10/50/100-point damage counters, and you can reset only that card's damage from the dialog. Drag a card to swap it between the bench and the active spot (its marker follows the same Pok\xe9mon). The Ability label at the bottom of each card is a manual reminder for whether that Pok\xe9mon's ability has been used. Tap it to switch between unused and used. It isn't reset automatically, so toggle it whenever it fits your situation."},
gIu(){return"Header buttons"},
gIt(){return"Refresh icon: after confirmation, resets that player's progress \u2014 damage, Special Conditions, Ability usage, Lost Zone, turn actions, and the GX/VSTAR marker's used flag (display and theme settings are not reset).\nCoin Toss: flips a coin.\nMenu (\u22ee):\n\u30fbAction History: review past actions, undo mistakes, or roll back the board to any previous point.\n\u30fbBattle Display: adjust bench slots (1\u20138) and choose markers.\n\u30fbEnd Battle: choose to either reset the field for the next battle or return to the home screen."},
gIA(){return"Special conditions"},
gIz(){return"Track Poison, Burn, Sleep, Paralysis, and Confusion. Sleep, Paralysis, and Confusion can only be active one at a time \u2014 choosing a new one clears the previous automatically. Poison and Burn can be combined with any of them."},
